t rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer Officia suscipit rer ','PUBLISHED','2025-09-10 09:35:12','2025-10-28 11:41:35',1,100.00,NULL,NULL),(8,'Hidden Gem of Poitry Canyon','Branson St, Branson, CO 81027, USA',202778.00,100,0,2447.00,'Legendary elk and mule deer hunting (Plains Elk Unit 136,5-month season,unlimited tags),Landowner deer and pronghorn antelope tags,Black bear,turkey,lion,and world-class predator hunting,Resident Rocky Mountain Bighorn Sheep',15000,'Discover the Hidden Gem of Poitry Canyon—an extraordinary ±2,447-acre legacy ranch steeped in history and adventure, now available for fractional ownership through Trophy Talk. This is the original headquarters of the famed Poitry Canyon Ranch, cherished by generations and newly released to the market for the first time in decades. Perfectly positioned in the heart of the renowned Plains Elk Units of Southeast Colorado, Hidden Gem Ranch is a true sanctuary for wildlife and a rare opportunity for discerning sportsmen and land stewards alike.\r\nA Hunter’s Paradise\r\nHidden Gem Ranch is a trophy hunter’s dream, boasting documented 360+ class bull elk and 200+ class mule deer that roam its vast, diverse terrain. The property sits within Plains Elk Unit 136, offering coveted 5-month hunting seasons from September 1 through January 31, with unlimited elk tags available for either sex and any weapon of choice. Landowner tags for mule deer and pronghorn antelope further enhance the ranch’s appeal, while over-the-counter opportunities abound for black bear, turkey, mountain lion, and world-class predator hunting. Keep your binoculars handy—resident Rocky Mountain Bighorn Sheep are known to frequent the ranch and neighboring canyons, adding to the unmatched wildlife experience.\r\nExceptional Land & Location\r\nLocated just 55 minutes east of I-25 and Trinidad in Las Animas County, Hidden Gem Ranch offers outstanding privacy with end-of-the-road seclusion and a locked gate entrance. A well-maintained county road ensures year-round access, while the ranch’s strategic lease to a local cattleman preserves valuable agricultural tax status. The landscape is a harmonious blend of rolling meadows, wooded canyons, and open grasslands, all well-watered by three productive wells, miles of waterlines and drinkers, multiple ponds, and robust fencing and cross-fencing throughout.\r\nQuality Improvements\r\nThe ranch headquarters is thoughtfully placed at the front of the property for easy access without impacting the ranch’s exceptional hunting grounds. The recently remodeled, fully furnished 3-bedroom, 2-bath ranch house features a classic Chisum Style decked front porch—ideal for relaxing after a day in the field—and a screened rear porch for quiet evenings. Both bathrooms have been newly upgraded, and fresh laminate flooring adds a modern touch to the home’s rustic charm.\r\nA standout feature is the impressive 4,080 sq. ft. two-story barn, designed for versatility and functionality. Half the barn boasts a concrete floor for equipment storage and projects, while the other half remains gravel for livestock or additional gear. Large bay doors provide easy access, and the barn includes a comfortable 2-bedroom guest apartment, a walk-in cold room for game processing, and a wash-down pad.\r\nAdding to the ranch’s historic character is the original hand-quarried stone homestead, nestled about a mile into the property near a year-round spring. With a recently remodeled roof and timeless stone exterior, this unique structure awaits your vision—whether as a guest retreat, hunting lodge, or a restoration project that honors the rich heritage of Southwest Colorado.\r\nThe Ultimate Ranch Experience\r\nHidden Gem Ranch is more than just land—it’s a lifestyle. Owners enjoy pro-rata access to all amenities, full hunting rights, and the peace of mind that comes with professional management by Trophy Talk, Inc. Whether you’re seeking world-class hunting, a family legacy property, or a private retreat surrounded by nature’s finest, Hidden Gem Ranch offers a rare and rewarding opportunity to own a piece of Colorado’s wild and storied landscape.\r\n','PUBLISHED','2025-09-11 21:24:47','2025-11-06 22:10:26',1,98.00,NULL,NULL),(9,'Country Cabin Land','Branson, CO 81027, USA',147300.00,20,0,1745.00,'Trophy-class wildlife,Headquarters,4080 SQ FT Barn,360+ bull elk and 200+ class mule deer.,5-month elk season (September 1–January 31),Landowner Deer Tags',15000,'Welcome to the Hidden Gem of Poitry Canyon—an iconic ±2,447-acre legacy ranch now available for fractional ownership at a remarkable value. This is the original headquarters of the Poitry Canyon Ranch, revered by hunters and outdoorsmen for generations and newly released to the market. Perfectly positioned in the heart of Colorado’s renowned Plains Elk Units, Hidden Gem Ranch is a rare sanctuary for wildlife, adventure, and investment.','PUBLISHED','2025-09-12 16:11:15','2025-11-06 22:10:23',1,99.00,'',''),(10,'New ranch','India',21100.00,100,0,2100.00,'Test one,Test two',11000,'Description is just for testing purposes!!!!','PUBLISHED','2025-09-24 16:00:49','2025-10-28 11:41:22',1,100.00,NULL,NULL),(11,'South Dakota Pheasant Acres','28146 382nd Ave, Armour, SD 57313, USA',480000.00,100,0,1800.00,'Breathtaking Property,1800-acre retreat,Turn-key property,World-class pheasant hunting,Premier whitetail deer,Unmatched waterfowl hunting,600 acres of food plots',15000,'Property Overview\r\nDiscover South Dakota Pheasant Acres Lodge, a breathtaking 1,800-acre retreat in the heart of South Dakota’s pheasant country. This turn-key property offers world-class pheasant hunting, rustic accommodations, and a rare opportunity for fractional ranch ownership. Designed for sportsmen and outdoor enthusiasts, this property blends adventure, tranquility, and rural luxury.\r\n\r\nLand & Amenities\r\nSouth Dakota’s oldest pheasant preserve with sculpted habitats\r\nPremier whitetail deer, waterfowl, and upland bird hunting\r\nTimber frame lodge with commercial kitchen and entertainment area\r\nTwo bunkhouse cabins, dog kennel, and pheasant brooding facility\r\nNearly 600 acres of food plots and multiple ponds/lakes\r\n\r\nHunting Opportunities & Tag Availability\r\nWhitetail Deer: Tags available via South Dakota Game, Fish & Parks lottery.\r\nArchery Season: Mid-September to December 31\r\nRifle Season (East River): Typically mid-November (check current SDGFP regulations)\r\nWaterfowl: Early teal opens early September; regular duck and goose seasons follow (consult SDGFP for annual dates).\r\nUpland Birds (Pheasant): Resident opener: early October; nonresident opener: mid-October. Season runs through early January (check SDGFP for exact dates).\r\n\r\nWhy South Dakota Pheasant Acres?\r\nExceptional whitetail, waterfowl, and upland bird habitat\r\nTurn-key lodge and hunting infrastructure\r\nProven wildlife management and food plot program\r\nUnique fractional ownership opportunity in a legacy property\r\n\r\nContact Trophy Talk for more information or to reserve your share in this premier South Dakota sporting estate.\r\n','PUBLISHED','2025-09-25 16:09:56','2025-10-28 11:41:26',1,100.00,NULL,NULL),(12,'South Dakota Pheasant Acres','28146 382nd Ave, Armour, SD 57313, USA',480000.00,30,0,1800.00,'1800-acre retreat,South Dakota’s oldest pheasant preserve,Premier whitetail deer,Waterfowl and upland bird hunting,Timber frame lodge,Nearly 600 acres of food plots and multiple ponds/lakes',15000,'Property Overview\r\n\r\nDiscover South Dakota Pheasant Acres Lodge, a breathtaking 1,800-acre retreat in the heart of South Dakota’s pheasant country. This turn-key property offers world-class pheasant hunting, rustic accommodations, and a rare opportunity for fractional ranch ownership. Designed for sportsmen and outdoor enthusiasts, this property blends adventure, tranquility, and rural luxury.\r\n\r\nHunting Opportunities & Tag Availability\r\n\r\nWhitetail Deer: Tags available via South Dakota Game, Fish & Parks lottery.\r\nArchery Season: Mid-September to December 31\r\nRifle Season (East River): Typically mid-November (check current SDGFP regulations)\r\n\r\nWaterfowl: Early teal opens early September; regular duck and goose seasons follow (consult SDGFP for annual dates).\r\n\r\nUpland Birds (Pheasant): Resident opener: early October; nonresident opener: mid-October. Season runs through early January (check SDGFP for exact dates).\r\n\r\nWhy South Dakota Pheasant Acres?\r\n\r\nExceptional whitetail, waterfowl, and upland bird habitat\r\n\r\nTurn-key lodge and hunting infrastructure\r\n\r\nProven wildlife management and food plot program\r\n\r\nUnique fractional ownership opportunity in a legacy property\r\n\r\nContact Trophy Talk for more information or to reserve your share in this premier South Dakota sporting estate.\r\n\r\n**This offering is expressly contingent upon Trophy Talk Management, LLC successfully securing the total purchase price and required capital raise for the acquisition of this property. If the necessary funds are not raised and the purchase price is not secured, this offering may be withdrawn or amended at the sole discretion of Trophy Talk Management, LLC.**','PUBLISHED','2025-09-26 18:45:05','2025-11-06 22:10:17',1,81.00,'',''),(13,'Cynthia Oneil','717 E 17th Ave, Columbus, OH 43211, USA',31.00,100,0,10000.00,'Justina Salinas',10,'Delectus ut consect','PUBLISHED','2025-10-07 10:51:09','2025-10-10 06: