ophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764385486835-1764385457500891.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764385489384-1764385457709140.jpg\"]','my south dakota trip and my deer','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-11-29 03:04:49','2025-11-29 03:04:49',NULL,0,0),(312,29,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764430500361-1764430499877585.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764430501286-1764430499998258.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764430501478-1764430500117990.jpg\"]','🦆','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-11-29 15:35:01','2025-11-29 15:35:01',NULL,0,0),(313,383,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764434537551-1764434534428663.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764434543921-1764434535024488.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764434553206-1764434535649625.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764434553756-1764434535996057.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764434555051-1764434536455385.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764434555591-1764434536797631.jpg\"]','Got a common merganser','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-11-29 16:42:39','2025-11-29 16:42:39',NULL,0,0),(315,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764556823243-1764556823096434.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764556823485-1764556823154211.jpg\"]','A buck I called wrap around. First spotted him as a 5.5 year old. I came to full drawn on him with my bow then for some reason decided to let him walk. Little did I know our game of cat and mouse would last 4 more years before coming to a close. After thousands of trail cam pics and a few sheds Wrap around and I finally finished our game on a brisk October morning in south Sask. He was 8.5 years old witch is a feet in itself to live that long as a whitetail evading hunters and predators and unforgiving Saskatchewan winters. At his peak he would have been close to 160” deer. He ended up scoring just over 150” as a 4x4 a true Sask King. #TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 02:40:23','2025-12-01 21:37:49',NULL,0,0),(316,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764556927091-1764556926965467.jpg\"]','A mule deer that’s as big as they get. I have found 2 sets of sheds off this buck but never once laid eyes on him. I named him Frank after Frank Abagnle Jr in catch me if you can. Frank was a master of Deception leaving only sheds behind to show he ever existed. I looked high and low for Frank and could never find him and many times he had me questioning my own sanity. I never heard of anyone else every laying eyes on Frank and as far as I know he was never shot either. I dream of one day stumbling upon a massive 250 plus inch non typical bleached out Mule deer buck skull laying on a side hill in the beautiful hills of South Saskatchewan laying in the same spot he took his last breath. #TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 02:42:07','2025-12-04 03:36:24',NULL,0,0),(318,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764557368824-1764557368630716.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764557369478-1764557368728294.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764557369673-1764557368765469.jpg\"]','My biggest whitetail to date a beautiful mature 164” sask beauty I got with my best hunting buddy. Me and Cody finally made it happen with the Muzzloader on a cold Sasky evening in October. Snuck in on this buck while we was in a group with 8 other bucks and a couple doe’s. We were frozen to the bone but made it into his kitchen un seen and put a good shot on him and down he went. #TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 02:49:29','2025-12-01 21:15:17',NULL,0,0),(320,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764557492095-1764557491988410.jpg\"]','Biggest buck I have been fortunate enough to be apart of. My friends and myself had 3 years of history with this buck and 3 years of sheds. We found him   as a 3.5 year old with all the potential in the world and got to witness first hand him grow into the 256” 6.5 year old king he turned out to be. I had the best seat in the house standing over my cousin Koles shoulder with my camera capturing the moment as he let his arrow fly. Good things take time if you trust the process and do it right the Gifts are that much better and mean that much more. #Booner #TrophyTalk','\"[Booner, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 02:51:32','2025-12-01 21:08:31',NULL,0,0),(322,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764557586912-1764557586790822.jpg\"]','#TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 02:53:07','2025-12-01 02:53:07',NULL,0,0),(324,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764558257111-1764558256795624.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764558257753-1764558256994484.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764558257899-1764558257020757.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764558257953-1764558257041564.jpg\"]','Found this buck in the summer months of 2021 and finally caught up to him September 15th. This buck lived in big country way in the hills and was very hard to keep tabs on. My Cousin Cody and I spotted him one evening after not seeing him for a couple weeks. We made a plan for the morning and spotted him way off in the hills with a big framed Typical he roamed around with. The two kings got the names Pauncho and lefty named after the country music Legends Willy and Waylon. We put many miles on the boots that day it was a roller coaster of a day one moment thinking the wheels fell off the bus and the next us finding our self 35 yards away as Pancho as he stood from his bed for a mid day stretch. I was at full draw with Cody over my shoulder with the camera and the rest is history. Pancho taped out at 222”. The Gifts the outdoors provide mean a lot more when you do it the right way and you earn it with your favourite people by your side. Pancho is just as much Cody’s as it’s mine. #Pancho  #TrophyTalk','\"[Pancho, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 03:04:18','2025-12-01 20:34:50',NULL,0,1),(325,58,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764562775066-1764562774698488.jpg\"]','Skinn old Grizz pilgrim?! Trophy Talk style!','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:19:38','2025-12-01 04:19:38',NULL,0,0),(326,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764562898228-1764562897892110.jpg\"]','The biggest typical mule deer I have ever harvested and probably ever will. I named this buck Big Rod after the land owner who’s land he called home. I first laid eyes on big Rod in late July standing proud in a flowering canola field, he was breath taking. Big Rod had disappeared like smart old bucks often do. I finally set eyes on him again September 27th. He lived in gnarly country and I knew sightings of the buck buck were going to be few and far between so I needed to make it count. I was able to close distance to 53 yards and my arrow hit its mark. Big Rod was truly world class with a Gross Score of 207” typical and a net score of 194net granting him Boone and Crocket all time status. He celetified a place in history as one of the biggest that have ever roamed the outdoor in the Boone and Crocket record book. Big Rod was largest Typical mule deer harvested with a bow in Saskatchewan in the 2020 season.  #Booner #TrophyTalk','\"[Booner, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:21:38','2025-12-01 19:06:20',NULL,0,0),(327,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764562946603-1764562946370321.jpg\"]','Old gray faced war horse I got with the bow. This buck had been on a downward slide in the horn department for a couple years at this point. But there is something to be said about matching wits and emerging yourself in a old warriors world and going head to head on his tearms. Matching your instincts as a hunter against a ancient old buck that has beat the odds for years with his instincts to survive hunters, predators and the harsh elements the outdoors provide. #TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:22:26','2025-12-01 18:39:36',NULL,0,0),(328,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764563021292-1764563020985380.jpg\"]','Poor man’s Sheep hunt #SpeedGoat #TrophyTalk','\"[SpeedGoat, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:23:42','2025-12-01 04:23:42',NULL,0,0),(329,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764563083227-1764563082989556.jpg\"]','Ancient old buck we called the Flyer buck myself and my friend group had been hunting this buck hard for 3 years with no luck the buck had ducked arrows and bullets on more than one occasion. The buck had not been seen in 2 years I had thought he fell to the hand of old man winter like many do. A friend and I were hunting the rut when I saw those classic flyers heading over a hill a site I haven’t seen in years. We made a move and a well placed shot put down the legend. We figured the flyer buck was 10.5 years old with very few teeth left. In his prime he was a 220” king the buck ended up scoring right at that 200” inch mark. He had about 8” of points broken off from still taking part in the battles of the rut even in his twilight years.  #FlyerBuck #TrophyTalk','\"[FlyerBuck, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:24:43','2025-12-01 18:23:29',NULL,0,0),(330,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764563361317-1764563360955930.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764563361591-1764563361030425.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764563361855-1764563361074226.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764563361900-1764563361102885.jpg\"]','The Gifts the outdoors provide are that much sweater when you embrace the process and respect and show empathy for the wildlife that calls the outdoors home. I had been running baits for around a decade. I start in July and bait through the fall and well into the winter months to help the deer get through the harsh winters that South Saskatchewan provides. The Goal has always been to harvest a mature whitetail buck with the bow. I watched this buck grow for 3 years before my arrow hit the mark ending our story. It was pretty special getting hundreds of photos of him through the years watching him grow from a 3.5 year old 5x5 with great potential to a beautiful mature buck. #TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:29:22','2025-12-01 18:04:40',NULL,0,0),(331,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764564037965-1764564037567619.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764564038508-1764564037608270.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764564039161-1764564037631651.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764564039560-1764564037652799.jpg\"]','My favourite buck to date and the one of the hardest most rewarding deer I have had the privilege of hunting. Had two years of History with this buck. I was fortunate enough to spend 46 days/ evenings in the summer of 2013 watching world class buck before finishing our last chapter on the 2nd day of Archery season. This buck jumped form a 178” buck to a 224” monster. A summer I will remember forever.  #FreakNasty #TrophyTalk','\"[FreakNasty, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:40:40','2025-12-01 17:49:50',NULL,0,1),(332,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764564337970-1764564337696797.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764564342675-1764564337777350.jpg\"]','A monster buck named King Kong my Cousn Cole and I hunted hard. Figured this old boy was around 8.5 years old with a blind milky eye that came along with the bloody battles he took part in to be the boss of his area for years. Kong is a rare buck breaking that 220” mark. #KingKong #TrophyTalk','\"[KingKong, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 04:45:51','2025-12-01 17:41:34',NULL,0,0),(333,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764568198364-1764568198193257.jpg\"]','Big Wide Fraimed Sask Mule deer. Our once world class mule deer hunting has taken a serious step back from the effects of CWD. The goal was to find a mature buck that was on the tail end of his Breading career. Those bucks are few and far between these days. I was lucky to find one that fit the bill. #TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 05:49:58','2025-12-01 17:32:56',NULL,0,0),(334,58,NULL,'https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/videos/1764569288736-058FAB42-1591-4C05-957F-F87C3C04BD74_L0_001_1764565514.830922_IMG_8165F9988FC9-A76D-4BA9-B745-569B0207E8F6.mp4','https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764569289311-058FAB42-1591-4C05-957F-F87C3C04BD74_L0_001_1764565514.830922_IMG_8165F9988FC9-A76D-4BA9-B745-569B0207E8F6.jpg','[]','Living that Trophy Talk lifestyle!','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','video',0,'2025-12-01 06:08:09','2025-12-01 07:45:53','6033.333333333333',0,1),(335,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764627242374-1764627241994441.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764627242904-1764627242141682.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764627243172-1764627242175842.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764627244039-1764627242265882.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764627244087-1764627242287281.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764627244099-1764627242314716.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764627244107-1764627242346473.jpg\"]','The story of Prince. When I first seen Price standing out in a chickpea field on a beautiful sask day he was a beautiful 5.5 year old 190” class buck with split backs and some stickers starting. We kept tabs on Prince seeing him regularly through the summer months but left him to grow. The next year he made a big jump into a massive framed buck we figured he was in that 215-220” range. I hunted him pretty hard early in the season than decided to change my focus to a large older typical I ended up shooting. I found Prince the following year and it appeared he had dropped about 10” but still was aweosome. I hunted him hard with a bow and he seemed to always be one step ahead of me. Cody and I finally caught up to him on a cold day in October he was in the bottom of a bowl with about 10 other deer with him. It seemed like an impossible stock but after belly crawling like coyotes for around 1500 yards we found our self’s around 120 yards away from Prince as he laid bedded in a slough. Cody was by my side with the camera as Price rose from his bed. A well placed shot with my Thompson Center Muzzloader ended the final chapter of my book with Prince. It’s an interesting complex feeling you get after killing a deer you have had a many year relationship with. Initially you feel a sense of excitement that all your work and dedication had paid off, than follows a sadness that it’s over. You watch them grow and mature into incredible animals and now you won’t ever get that enjoyment of watching him stand proud like the king he was in the wilderness like you had many times before. Very few know what I’m talking about but the ones that do understand completely. #NaturesGifts #TrophyTalk','\"[NaturesGifts, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-01 22:14:04','2025-12-01 22:14:04',NULL,0,0),(336,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764885156501-1764885156354919.jpg\"]','If you were ever wondering what 20” G2s look like. #TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-04 21:52:36','2025-12-04 21:52:36',NULL,0,0),(337,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764885446411-1764885446235939.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764885446540-1764885446287520.jpg\"]','Saskatchewan Booner','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-04 21:57:26','2025-12-04 21:57:26',NULL,0,0),(338,379,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764909204735-1764909202597433.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764909204801-1764909202712973.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764909204867-1764909203053449.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764909204924-1764909203209316.jpg\"]','Younger yrs','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-05 04:33:25','2025-12-09 13:06:39',NULL,0,1),(340,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764914229053-1764914228579207.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764914230102-1764914228765035.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764914231057-1764914228894162.jpg\"]','#Sheds #TrophyTalk','\"[Sheds, TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-05 05:57:12','2025-12-05 05:57:12',NULL,0,0),(341,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764914548966-1764914548853684.jpg\"]','#TrophyTalk','\"[TrophyTalk]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-05 06:02:29','2025-12-05 06:02:29',NULL,0,0),(342,384,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1764914869254-1764914869142129.jpg\"]','#BigBoy','\"[BigBoy]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-05 06:07:49','2025-12-05 06:07:49',NULL,0,0),(343,379,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246307781-1765246303443264.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246307950-1765246303621679.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246308070-1765246303827170.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246308115-1765246304007925.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246308160-1765246304190814.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246308222-1765246304394679.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246308284-1765246304555414.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246308365-1765246304887890.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765246308655-1765246305221796.jpg\"]','A few good hunts','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-09 02:11:49','2025-12-09 13:07:47',NULL,0,1),(344,398,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765298569130-1765298568675293.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765298570525-1765298568798530.jpg\"]','Think the smile says it all, even cooler that the trail camera caught the first look after the harvest!  His personal best at 175” #whitetail','\"[whitetail]\"','Gatesville','null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-09 16:42:50','2025-12-09 16:42:50',NULL,0,0),(345,398,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765299065836-1765299065040794.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765299067528-1765299065099298.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765299067970-1765299065128082.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765299068322-1765299065147904.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765299068911-1765299065188270.jpg\"]','EPIC honeymoon trip to New Zealand in 2020!  Red Stag was 520” and the Bull Elk was 421”. \n\nEven after the hunt, the fun continued as we flew home with our extra checked “bags” 😂\n\n#honeymoon #newzealand #stag #elk','\"[honeymoon, newzealand, stag, elk]\"','New Zealand','null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-09 16:51:09','2025-12-09 16:51:09',NULL,0,0),(346,398,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765378519070-1765378518209887.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765378520474-1765378518343523.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765378520687-1765378518353692.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765378522180-1765378518571864.jpg\",\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765378523983-1765378518790774.jpg\"]','Most folks have never even thought about eating zebra—but it’s delicious, lean, and unforgettable.  Have you had? \n#Zebra #FieldToFork','\"[Zebra, FieldToFork]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-10 14:55:25','2025-12-10 14:55:25',NULL,0,0),(347,17,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765383714645-1765383714456554.jpg\"]','Congrats Joe on a successful Kansas hunt!','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-10 16:21:56','2025-12-10 16:21:56',NULL,0,0),(348,58,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765459446803-1765459446487677.jpg\"]','Morning sunrises in deer camp just hit different!','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-11 13:24:09','2025-12-11 13:24:09',NULL,0,0),(349,17,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[\"https://trophy-talk-bucket.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/images/1765494465915-1765494465425492.jpg\"]','Afternoon’s in Kansas','\"[]\"',NULL,'null','Everyone','image',0,'2025-12-11 23:07:48','2025-12-11 23:07:48',NULL,0,0);
